.TH "NAVIGATOR.SERIAL" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Navigator.serial \- Navigator: serial property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]serial\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]Navigator\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Serial\f[R] object, which
represents the entry point into the Web Serial API.
.PP
The same instance of the \f[CR]Serial\f[R] object will always be
returned.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]Serial\f[R] object.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS List available ports
The following example uses the \f[CR]getPorts()\f[R] method to
initialize a list of available ports.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serial.getPorts().then((ports) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// Initialize the list of available ports with \(gaports\(ga on page load.\f[R]
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\c
